#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1096
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "What `Fly.io` actually billed for one month, copied from the invoice, so the estimate of that month stands next to the real sum."
msgstr "Koliko je `Fly.io` zaista naplatio za jedan mesec, prepisano sa računa, da procena tog meseca stoji pored pravog iznosa."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:2133
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "`Fly.io` gives no way to read its bills, so Potok estimates them itself. Every quarter of an hour it reads which machines run and how big they are, how big the database and the stored files are and how much data went out, and writes what each <CostHour>hour</CostHour> cost by the price list. The hours it missed, back to the start of the month, are filled in from `Fly.io`'s own metrics of those hours, which go back about ten days, and the rest from what runs now. Once a month is billed, one of the people who run Potok copies the sum from the <Invoice>invoice</Invoice>, and only they may. Everyone with an account sees both on the costs page; guests do not."
msgstr "`Fly.io` ne daje način da se pročitaju njegovi računi, pa ih Potok sam procenjuje. Na svakih petnaest minuta pročita koje mašine rade i koliko su velike, koliko su veliki baza i sačuvani fajlovi i koliko je podataka poslato, pa upiše koliko je svaki <CostHour>sat</CostHour> koštao po cenovniku. Sate koje je propustio, sve do početka meseca, popuni iz metrika samog `Fly.io` za te sate, koje sežu desetak dana unazad, a ostalo iz onoga što radi sada. Kad mesec bude naplaćen, neko od onih koji vode Potok prepiše iznos sa <Invoice>računa</Invoice>, i to smeju samo oni. Oboje na strani sa troškovima vidi svako ko ima nalog, a gosti ne."

