msgstr "prečica u listi"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:736
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Entity definition"
msgstr "Definicija entiteta"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1359
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "The attributes are kept as a list."
msgstr "Atributi se čuvaju kao lista."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:443
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "attributes and their types"
msgstr "atributi i njihovi tipovi"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:928
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "What the data of the processes drawn in a group looks like, as its editors define it: a name and up to 30 attributes, each with the type of what it holds. An attribute holds a text, a number, a yes or no, a date, a date and time, one of the choices it lists, or another entity of the group, and may be a list of them. Entities nest at most four deep and never in a circle. A group has at most 50, each name once in any letter case, and one that another holds, or that a process drawn in the group keeps a variable of, cannot be deleted. Deleting the group takes them along."
msgstr "Kako izgledaju podaci procesa nacrtanih u grupi, onako kako ih njeni urednici definišu: ime i najviše 30 atributa, svaki sa tipom onoga što sadrži. Atribut sadrži tekst, broj, da ili ne, datum, datum i vreme, jedan od izbora koje navodi ili drugi entitet grupe, a može da bude i lista. Entiteti se ugnežđuju najviše četiri nivoa duboko i nikad ukrug. Grupa ima najviše 50 entiteta, svako ime jednom, bez obzira na velika i mala slova, a entitet koji drugi sadrži, ili čiju varijablu čuva proces nacrtan u grupi, ne može da se obriše. Brisanje grupe briše i njih."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:480
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "what its variables hold"
msgstr "šta mu varijable drže"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:2041
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "A <AppProcess>process</AppProcess> drawn in Potok that starts on a call, on a signal, by hand or on a value may take an <GroupEntity>entity</GroupEntity> of its group. A call then hands it that entity's attributes, each a value of its type and every required one a value, checked when the caller is saved and again when the call is made, against the entity as the called process was saved with it; a call that does not fit fails where it stands and starts nothing. A process started by hand asks for the attributes in a form, lists and the entities it holds included. A signal is waited for with an entity, and a process sends it only with the entity those who wait for it expect, where someone does: whoever waits says what it waits for. A drawing whose entity changed since it was saved, or whose calls and signals no longer fit those they talk to, runs on as it was saved, and its editors are told to look it over."
msgstr "Nacrtan <AppProcess>proces</AppProcess> koji počinje na poziv, na signal, ručno ili na vrednost može da prima <GroupEntity>entitet</GroupEntity> svoje grupe. Poziv mu tada predaje atribute tog entiteta, svakom vrednost njegovog tipa i svakom obaveznom neku vrednost, što se proverava kad se pozivalac čuva i ponovo kad se poziv desi, prema entitetu kakav je bio kad je pozvani proces sačuvan; poziv koji ne odgovara pada tu gde stoji i ne pokreće ništa. Proces koji se pokreće ručno atribute traži u formi, uz liste i entitete koje drži. Signal se čeka sa entitetom, a proces ga šalje samo sa entitetom koji očekuju oni koji ga čekaju, ako takvih ima: ko čeka, kaže šta čeka. Crtež čiji se entitet promenio otkad je sačuvan, ili čiji pozivi i signali više ne odgovaraju onima sa kojima razgovara, radi kako je sačuvan, a njegovim urednicima se kaže da ga pregledaju."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:2039
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "What a process takes is an entity"
msgstr "Ono što proces prima je entitet"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:399
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "entity it takes"
msgstr "entitet koji prima"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:2033
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Besides the process an app writes into its rules, the editors of a group can draw processes of their own in Potok, as <AppProcess>app processes</AppProcess> that keep their graph outside any app's settings. One starts on a new value of a collection of an app, on a member's chat message holding one of its words or mentioning its role, on a sub-group made one at a time (not a record, a thread or what a process makes), on a schedule, when someone holding its role starts it by hand with a title and a text, when another process drawn in the group calls it, or on a signal one sends. An app replaces its settings whole when it saves them, so it could never keep a drawing safe; this way it neither sees nor overwrites them, and its own process runs beside them. A drawing is kept only when an instance could finish it, with roles the group has, and starts switched off. What its texts and conditions say are expressions over the names it has, such as what set it going and what a decision ended with, checked when it is kept, so a drawing that names what is not there is refused. One kept before expressions is turned into them when its editor opens it, and an instance reads the language of the graph it started with. A drawing may also declare variables, each with the type of what it holds, a plain one or an <GroupEntity>entity</GroupEntity> of the group: a step sets one to what an expression gives, every instance keeps its own, and the drawing is kept with the entities as they were then, so an instance under way reads them the same after one changes. A step may also go through a list an item at a time, with steps of its own for each: it reads the list once, on its way in, at most 200 items, and hands each to those steps by a name. So that a drawing that runs in a circle stops, an instance takes at most 25 steps in a row without waiting, counted anew for each item, and 5,000 in its life; after 100 it gives way to the others, and the steps that write outside it (a message, a sub-group, a push, a field of the group, a signal, a call) are 60 a minute for a process at most. Switched on, its profile joins the group and each of these starts a <ValueProcess>process instance</ValueProcess> of it; a change applies to the instances that start after it, and switching it off cancels those that run or wait. The app knows nothing of their tasks, so the people of a task's role finish them on the group's Processes tab, where they see a <Value>value</Value> only as far as they may read it. Deleting the app takes the processes drawn on its collections along."
msgstr "Pored procesa koji aplikacija upisuje u svoja pravila, urednici grupe mogu u Potoku da nacrtaju i svoje procese, kao <AppProcess>procese aplikacije</AppProcess> čiji graf stoji van podešavanja bilo koje aplikacije. Takav proces počinje na novoj vrednosti u kolekciji aplikacije, na poruci člana u razgovoru koja ima neku od njegovih reči ili pominje njegovu ulogu, na podgrupi napravljenoj jedna po jedna (ne na zapisu, niti ni onome što napravi proces), po rasporedu, kad ga neko sa njegovom ulogom pokrene ručno, uz naslov i tekst, kad ga pozove drugi proces nacrtan u grupi, ili na signal koji neki pošalje. Aplikacija pri čuvanju zameni cela podešavanja, pa crtež tamo ne bi bio bezbedan. Ovako ga aplikacija ne vidi i ne može da ga pregazi, a njen proces radi pored nacrtanih. Čuva se samo crtež koji instanca može da završi, sa ulogama koje grupa ima, i nastaje isključen. Ono što njegovi tekstovi i uslovi kažu su izrazi nad imenima koja proces ima, kao što su ono što ga je pokrenulo i ishod odluke, i proveravaju se pri čuvanju, pa se crtež koji imenuje nešto čega nema odbija. Crtež sačuvan pre izraza prevodi se u njih kad ga urednik otvori, a instanca čita zapis grafa sa kojim je krenula. Crtež može da ima i varijable, svaku sa tipom onoga što drži, običnim ili <GroupEntity>entitetom</GroupEntity> grupe: korak varijabli daje ono što izraz izračuna, svaka instanca ima svoje, a crtež se čuva sa entitetima kakvi su tada bili, pa ih instanca u toku čita isto i kad se neki promeni. Korak može i da prođe kroz listu, stavku po stavku, sa svojim koracima za svaku: listu čita jednom, kad u nju uđe, najviše 200 stavki, i svaku tim koracima daje pod imenom. Da bi crtež koji se vrti ukrug stao, instanca pravi najviše 25 koraka zaredom bez čekanja, što se za svaku stavku broji iznova, i 5.000 za svog veka; posle 100 ustupa mesto drugima, a koraka koji pišu van nje (poruka, podgrupa, push, polje grupe, signal, poziv) proces ima najviše 60 u minutu. Kad se uključi, njegov profil ulazi u grupu, a svaki od tih događaja pokreće njegovu <ValueProcess>instancu procesa</ValueProcess>. Izmena važi za instance koje krenu posle nje, a isključivanje otkazuje one koje rade ili čekaju. Aplikacija ne zna za njihove zadatke, pa ih ljudi sa ulogom zadatka završavaju na kartici Procesi u grupi, gde <Value>vrednost</Value> vide samo koliko smeju da je čitaju. Brisanje aplikacije briše i procese nacrtane na njenim kolekcijama."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:2069
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "A drawn <AppProcess>process</AppProcess> that others call is private until an editor makes it public. A private one is called by the processes of its own <Group>group</Group> alone. A public one is called from the groups above its group and from those below it too, never from a branch beside it, and the editors there see its name and what it takes. The <ValueProcess>run</ValueProcess> such a call starts in another group gets what the call hands over and nothing else: it has no subject and nobody set it off, as the caller's value and people are no part of that group, and the caller hears only which end it reached. Callers of other groups do not keep a public process from being deleted or made private again: their calls then fail where they stand, their editors are told to look the drawing over, and a caller left waiting for a run that went with its group fails as one whose run was cancelled."
msgstr "Nacrtan <AppProcess>proces</AppProcess> koji drugi pozivaju privatan je dok ga urednik ne učini javnim. Privatan pozivaju samo procesi njegove <Group>grupe</Group>. Javan pozivaju i procesi grupa iznad njegove grupe i onih ispod nje, nikad iz grane pored, a urednici tamo vide njegovo ime i šta prima. <ValueProcess>Pokretanje</ValueProcess> koje takav poziv napravi u drugoj grupi dobija ono što mu poziv preda i ništa više: nema predmet i niko ga nije pokrenuo, jer vrednost i ljudi pozivaoca nisu deo te grupe, a pozivalac saznaje samo do kog kraja je stiglo. Pozivaoci iz drugih grupa ne sprečavaju da se javan proces obriše ili ponovo postane privatan: njihovi pozivi tada padaju tu gde stoje, njihovim urednicima se kaže da pregledaju crtež, a pozivalac koji je ostao da čeka pokretanje nestalo sa svojom grupom pada kao onaj čije je pokretanje otkazano."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:2064
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "A process is private to its group, or public up and down the tree"
msgstr "Proces je privatan u svojoj grupi, ili javan uz i niz stablo"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1305
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Only a process drawn in Potok that another calls can be public."
msgstr "Javan može da bude samo proces nacrtan u Potoku koji drugi poziva."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:486
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "person its wait asks"
msgstr "osoba koju čekanje pita"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:483
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "role its wait asks"
msgstr "uloga koju čekanje pita"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:2055
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "A process asks a person with a form"
msgstr "Proces pita čoveka formom"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:2057
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "A step of a drawing may be a form: it stops the <ValueProcess>process instance</ValueProcess> until a person fills in an <GroupEntity>entity</GroupEntity>, each attribute as its type, a list a row per item and an entity it holds as a group of its own, as the drawing was saved with it. It may say something first, and start with something in some attributes, worked out from what the instance holds when the form is opened; the person may change it, and what they send counts. It asks whoever started the instance, or the people of a role, and only a member of the group answers, once. The form opens by itself only for the one who started the instance, and only when it was their own step that led to it: a message they wrote, a start by hand, a form before it. Reached after a wait or someone else's decision, and for a role, it waits on the group's Processes tab. What was filled in is read by the steps that follow, an attribute at a time, with who filled it in, and whoever filled it in sets off those steps. Nobody starts a process on a schedule, so its form asks a role, and an instance nobody started fails on a form that asks whoever did. While it waits for a person, on a form or a decision, an instance keeps whom it asks, so a group's page counts what waits for its viewer without reading every waiting instance, and counts again only on news that is theirs. The same count stands on the bar's hand beside the join requests the person may approve, the Requests page lists those tasks by group, and an amber mark stands on the rows of the groups they wait in and of those above them."
msgstr "Korak crteža može biti forma: zaustavlja <ValueProcess>instancu procesa</ValueProcess> dok čovek ne popuni <GroupEntity>entitet</GroupEntity>, svaki atribut po svom tipu, listu red po red, a entitet koji drži kao posebnu celinu, onakav sa kakvim je crtež sačuvan. Može prvo nešto da kaže, a u nekim atributima već nešto može da bude upisano, izračunato iz onoga što instanca ima kad se forma otvori; čovek to može da promeni, a važi ono što pošalje. Pita onoga ko je instancu pokrenuo, ili ljude neke uloge, a odgovara samo član grupe, jednom. Forma se sama otvara samo onome ko je instancu pokrenuo, i samo kad je do nje doveo njegov korak: poruka koju je napisao, ručno pokretanje, forma pre nje. Kad do nje dođe posle čekanja ili tuđe odluke, i kad pita ulogu, čeka na kartici Procesi u grupi. Ono što je popunjeno čitaju koraci koji slede, atribut po atribut, uz to ko je popunio, a ko je popunio pokreće te korake. Proces po rasporedu ne pokreće niko, pa njegova forma pita ulogu, a instanca koju niko nije pokrenuo pada na formi koja pita pokretača. Dok čeka čoveka, na formi ili na odluci, instanca pamti koga pita, pa stranica grupe broji šta čeka onoga ko je gleda bez čitanja svake instance koja čeka, i broji ponovo samo na vest koja je njegova. Isti broj stoji na ruci u gornjoj traci, uz zahteve za pristup koje čovek može da odobri, stranica Zahtevi nabraja te zadatke po grupama, a ćilibarna oznaka stoji na redovima grupa u kojima čekaju i onih iznad njih."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1913
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "A <GroupMembership>membership</GroupMembership> remembers until when its member silenced the group: an hour, eight hours, a week or until they turn it on again. Until then nothing that goes to everyone reaches them as a push: new values, polls, events, an app's notices, a process's push to everyone. What is meant for them still does: a mention, an answer to their value, a reaction, a process asking them or their role. The group's unread values leave the home badge and the sums of the groups above it, while its own row still shows them, in grey. The threads of a silenced group are silent too."
msgstr "<GroupMembership>Članstvo</GroupMembership> pamti do kada je član utišao grupu: na sat vremena, osam sati, nedelju dana ili dok je ponovo ne uključi. Do tada mu nijedan push koji ide svima ne stiže: nove vrednosti, glasanja, događaji, obaveštenja aplikacije, push procesa svima. Ono što je namenjeno njemu i dalje stiže: pominjanje, odgovor na njegovu vrednost, reakcija, proces koji pita njega ili njegovu ulogu. Nepročitane vrednosti grupe izlaze iz broja na kućici i iz zbirova grupa iznad nje, a njen red ih i dalje pokazuje, sivo. Utišana grupa utišava i svoje niti."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1911
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "A member can silence a group"
msgstr "Član može da utiša grupu"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:489
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "until when the member silenced it"
msgstr "do kada je član utišao grupu"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:2049
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "A <AppProcess>process</AppProcess> that others call may name an <GroupEntity>entity</GroupEntity> of its group that it hands back. Each of its ends then fills it in, an attribute at a time, checked when the process is saved, and the caller reads it under the call's id, in its own group or in another: the process hands over exactly that and nothing else. One that names none hands back only the end it reached, and to a caller of its own group what it was given and what its waits brought back. An end whose values do not fit when the run gets there fails that run, and the caller waits for it as for any run it called."
msgstr "<AppProcess>Proces</AppProcess> koji drugi pozivaju može da navede <GroupEntity>entitet</GroupEntity> svoje grupe koji vraća. Tada ga svaki njegov kraj popunjava, atribut po atribut, što se proverava kad se proces sačuva, a pozivalac ga čita pod id-jem poziva, u svojoj grupi ili u drugoj: proces predaje tačno to i ništa više. Proces koji ne navede nijedan vraća samo kraj do kog je stigao, a pozivaocu iz svoje grupe i ono što je dobio i ono što su mu čekanja donela. Kraj čije vrednosti ne odgovaraju kad tok stigne do njega obara taj tok, a pozivalac ga čeka kao svaki tok koji je pozvao."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:2047
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "A called process can hand an entity back"
msgstr "Pozvani proces može da vrati entitet"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:405
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "entity it hands back"
msgstr "entitet koji vraća"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:375
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "file name as a search reads it, in Latin and without diacritics"
msgstr "naziv fajla kako ga pretraga čita, latinicom i bez kvačica"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:900
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "A group a profile keeps at the top of its column of groups. Only that profile sees it. Deleting the group or the profile takes it along."
msgstr "Grupa koju profil drži na vrhu svoje kolone grupa. Vidi je samo taj profil. Brisanje grupe ili profila briše i nju."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1945
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Beside a group's page, a wide screen shows the profile's groups as a tree: its <GroupMembership>memberships</GroupMembership>, the public groups it <GroupFollow>follows</GroupFollow> and the <Group>groups</Group> on the way to them, without threads or the records apps keep as groups; direct conversations stand in a list of their own below it. A closed folder counts everything unread below it, an open one only what its open sub-groups do not show, so every unread value can be followed down to its group. Above the tree stand the <PinnedGroup>pinned groups</PinnedGroup>: up to 20 groups the profile sees, never the root or a direct conversation, in the order it pinned them. Nobody else sees them, and a group it no longer sees drops out of the list. A narrower screen opens the same tree in a panel from a button in the group's header, and the pinned groups also stand at the top of the root's list of groups."
msgstr "Pored stranice grupe, širok ekran pokazuje grupe profila kao stablo: njegova <GroupMembership>članstva</GroupMembership>, javne grupe koje <GroupFollow>prati</GroupFollow> i <Group>grupe</Group> na putu do njih, bez niti i zapisa koje aplikacije čuvaju kao grupe; direktni razgovori stoje u svojoj listi ispod. Zatvoren folder broji sve nepročitano ispod sebe, a otvoren samo ono što njegove otvorene podgrupe ne pokazuju, pa se svaka nepročitana vrednost može pratiti do svoje grupe. Iznad stabla stoje <PinnedGroup>prikačene grupe</PinnedGroup>: do 20 grupa koje profil vidi, nikad koren ni direktan razgovor, redom kojim ih je prikačio. Niko drugi ih ne vidi, a grupa koju više ne vidi ispada iz liste. Uži ekran otvara isto stablo u panelu, dugmetom u zaglavlju grupe, a prikačene grupe stoje i na vrhu liste grupa korena."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:731
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Pinned group"
msgstr "Prikačena grupa"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1943
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "The column of your groups is a tree"
msgstr "Kolona tvojih grupa je stablo"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:502
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "who pinned it"
msgstr "ko ju je prikačio"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:598
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "reactions by emoji, with how many and the first names"
msgstr "reakcije po emodžiju, sa brojem i prvim imenima"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:259
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "member count in a list of sub-groups"
msgstr "broj članova u spisku podgrupa"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1817
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "A <Group>group</Group> opened from a <Value>value</Value> is a thread. One value has at most one thread. A thread inherits from its group only those who take part in it: whoever opened it, the author of its value, and a member of the group who opens it, writes in it or is mentioned in it. They hold the roles they hold in the group and leave with it. There is one root, with no parent and no creator. All other groups have both, even direct conversations, which sit right under the root."
msgstr "<Group>Grupa</Group> otvorena iz <Value>vrednosti</Value> je nit. Jedna vrednost ima najviše jednu nit. Nit od svoje grupe nasleđuje samo one koji u njoj učestvuju: onoga ko ju je otvorio, autora njene vrednosti i člana grupe koji je otvori, piše u njoj ili je u njoj pomenut. Oni u njoj imaju uloge koje imaju u grupi i izlaze iz nje kad izađu iz grupe. Koren je jedan, bez roditelja i bez autora. Sve ostale grupe imaju oboje, pa i direktni razgovori, koji stoje odmah ispod korena."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1905
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "A <GroupValueRead>read marker</GroupValueRead> holds, for one profile in one group, the last <Value>value</Value> it has read, and everything newer is unread. Only members have one, and a chat opened while still empty gets one too. Whoever joins, by an invitation, a request or through the parent, gets it at the newest value, so the history is there to read but not counted. Opening the chat moves the marker to the newest value, and the line that shows where the unread values begin stands where the marker was before. A group counts at most 100 unread values, shown as 99+, and every sum above it adds what its groups counted. A group's newest value shows in the lists only to its members, as only their pages hear of new values. A search of the chat finds what the chat shows: a member's also takes the group's threads, and someone reading an open chat from outside does not find announcements of events that are not public."
msgstr "<GroupValueRead>Marker čitanja</GroupValueRead> čuva, za jedan profil u jednoj grupi, poslednju <Value>vrednost</Value> koju je pročitao, a sve novije je nepročitano. Imaju ga samo članovi, a dobija ga i razgovor otvoren dok je još prazan. Ko uđe, pozivnicom, zahtevom ili preko roditelja, dobija ga na najnovijoj vrednosti, pa je istorija tu da se čita, ali se ne broji. Otvaranje razgovora pomera marker na najnoviju vrednost, a linija koja pokazuje gde počinju nepročitane vrednosti stoji tamo gde je marker bio pre toga. Grupa broji najviše 100 nepročitanih vrednosti, prikazano kao 99+, a svaki zbir iznad nje sabira ono što su njene grupe izbrojale. Najnovija vrednost grupe vidi se u listama samo njenim članovima, jer samo njihove stranice čuju za nove vrednosti. Pretraga razgovora nalazi ono što razgovor pokazuje: pretraga člana uzima i niti grupe, a ko čita otvoren razgovor spolja ne nalazi najave događaja koji nisu javni."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1123
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "A thread always inherits from its group, taking its members in as they take part."
msgstr "Nit uvek nasleđuje od svoje grupe, a njene članove prima kako učestvuju."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:492
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "the last of its values the member got a push for"
msgstr "poslednja vrednost grupe o kojoj je član dobio push obaveštenje"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:495
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "when it last pushed the member"
msgstr "kada je član poslednji put dobio push obaveštenje iz grupe"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1921
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "A <GroupMembership>membership</GroupMembership> also remembers the last of the group's <Value>values</Value> its member got a push for, and when. The next value of the group pushes them again only once they have read up to that one, or five minutes later. Picking the members and marking them is one statement, so values posted at the same moment still make one push. A mention and an answer to their value always go out and leave the mark as it was. A thread waits on its own, with its own memberships. Polls, events, reminders, notices, reactions and a process's pushes are not held back."
msgstr "<GroupMembership>Članstvo</GroupMembership> pamti i poslednju <Value>vrednost</Value> grupe o kojoj je član dobio push obaveštenje, i kada. Sledeća vrednost iste grupe šalje mu push tek kad pročita do nje, ili posle pet minuta. Izbor i obeležavanje članova su jedna izjava baze, pa i vrednosti poslate u istom trenutku daju jedan push. Pominjanje i odgovor na njegovu vrednost stižu uvek i ne menjaju to pamćenje. Nit čeka zasebno, sa svojim članstvima. Glasanja, događaji, podsetnici, obaveštenja, reakcije i push procesa se ne zadržavaju."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1919
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "A group pushes once until it is read"
msgstr "Grupa šalje jedan push dok se ne pročita"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:769
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Tokens of sessions and of links in emails, such as log-in, invitation and email change. Each token says what it is for, and once no check accepts it any more, it is deleted."
msgstr "Tokeni sesija i linkova iz imejlova, kao što su prijava, pozivnica i promena imejla. Svaki token kaže čemu služi, a kad ga nijedna provera više ne prihvata, briše se."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:2025
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "When a <Value>value</Value> comes to a collection whose process has a graph, a <ValueProcess>process instance</ValueProcess> starts in the same transaction, with a copy of the graph, so changing the rule later leaves it as it was. Each element runs in a transaction of its own together with the instance's move to the next, so what it writes happens once. The instance waits on a task until someone holding the task's role picks an outcome or the deadline passes, and on a timer until it is due; a scheduler on every server takes forward those whose time has come. An action that fails leaves the instance failed where it stopped, for an editor to take up again, and removing the rule cancels the instances that run or wait. A month after an instance ends, done or cancelled, it keeps its status and log but not the copy of the graph, its variables or what it started from; a failed one keeps everything, for a retry. Nobody learns from a process who wrote an anonymous value."
msgstr "Kad <Value>vrednost</Value> stigne u kolekciju čiji proces ima graf, u istoj transakciji nastaje <ValueProcess>instanca procesa</ValueProcess>, sa kopijom grafa, pa kasnija izmena pravila ne menja nju. Svaki element se izvršava u svojoj transakciji, zajedno sa pomeranjem instance na sledeći, pa ono što napiše nastaje jednom. Instanca čeka na zadatku dok neko sa ulogom zadatka ne izabere ishod ili ne istekne rok, a na tajmeru dok ne dođe vreme; Scheduler na svakom serveru pokreće one kojima je vreme došlo. Akcija koja ne uspe ostavlja instancu palu tamo gde je stala, da je urednik ponovo pokrene, a uklanjanje pravila otkazuje instance koje rade ili čekaju. Mesec dana posle kraja, završena ili otkazana instanca zadržava status i dnevnik, ali ne i kopiju grafa, promenljive i ono sa čim je krenula; neuspela zadržava sve, za ponovni pokušaj. Niko iz procesa ne saznaje ko je napisao anonimnu vrednost."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1130
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Only a group that inherits members, and is not a thread, picks roles to inherit them by."
msgstr "Uloge po kojima nasleđuje članove bira samo grupa koja ih nasleđuje, a nije nit."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:214
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "roles it inherits by"
msgstr "uloge po kojima nasleđuje"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1618
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "It gets the <Group>groups</Group> right under it that have a place on a map, with the pin each one shows, and whoever may make a sub-group there can add one where they tap. A tap on a pin opens that group's description over the app, where its own app, a form or a poll, works with that group's rights. Among them, groups that cover an area come with their borders, groups that run along a route with their lines and lengths, and each place with the areas it lies in or passes through, so the app draws the areas and routes and shows only the groups inside one area. A map of more than 2000 places gets only what its view shows, which the server gathers into numbered circles as on the root's map, filtered by name and by the pins the groups show. That is how a group becomes a map. The root needs no such app: it has a map of its own. Any app can also take the viewer to the root's map at a point it keeps in its own data, such as a farm or where goods are handed out, with the group's picture on the pin: the group's own place stays as it is."
msgstr "Dobija <Group>grupe</Group> neposredno ispod sebe koje imaju mesto na mapi, sa pinom koji svaka pokazuje, a ko tu sme da pravi podgrupe može da doda novu tamo gde dodirne. Dodir na pin otvara opis te grupe preko aplikacije, gde njena aplikacija, forma ili glasanje, radi sa pravima te grupe. Među njima grupe koje pokrivaju područje stižu sa svojim granicama, grupe koje idu rutom sa njenom linijom i dužinom, a svako mesto sa područjima u kojima je ili kroz koja prolazi, pa aplikacija crta područja i rute i pokazuje samo grupe unutar jednog područja. Mapa sa više od 2000 mesta dobija samo ono što pokazuje njen pogled, a server to skuplja u numerisane krugove kao na mapi korena, uz filter po nazivu i po pinovima koje grupe pokazuju. Tako grupa postaje mapa. Korenu takva aplikacija ne treba: on ima svoju mapu. Svaka aplikacija može i da odvede gledaoca na mapu korena, do tačke koju čuva u svojim podacima, recimo do proizvođača ili mesta gde se roba deli, sa slikom grupe na pinu: mesto same grupe ostaje kakvo jeste."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1729
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "A site inside an app gets the theme, the language and the calls its description lists, and no more. Potok cannot tell which page stands in that frame, so the list holds for whatever opens there."
msgstr "Sajt u aplikaciji dobija temu, jezik i pozive koje njen opis nabroji, i ništa više. Potok ne može da zna koja je stranica u tom okviru, pa lista važi za sve što se tu otvori."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1679
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Shows a site"
msgstr "Prikazuje sajt"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1807
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "A deleted account leaves what was written"
msgstr "Obrisan nalog ostavlja ono što je napisano"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:181
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "person, process or deleted"
msgstr "osoba, proces ili obrisan"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1681
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "A description can show a site from another address, in a frame inside its own. Potok tells that site the viewer's theme and language, so the site can follow them, and passes on only the calls the description lists for it. It remembers the page the reader got to, and a link to the group can open a chapter of the site. That is how a handbook published elsewhere reads as a part of the group."
msgstr "Opis može da prikaže sajt sa druge adrese, u okviru unutar svog. Potok tom sajtu javlja temu i jezik gledaoca, pa sajt može da ih prati, i prosleđuje mu samo pozive koje opis za njega nabroji. Pamti stranicu do koje je čitalac stigao, a link na grupu može da otvori poglavlje sajta. Tako se priručnik objavljen drugde čita kao deo grupe."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1690
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "An app, or a site in its frame, keeps a <AppProfileEntry>personal memory</AppProfileEntry> for each viewer: how far they read, what they marked. It is the same on every device and only that person reads it, not even the app's editors; a guest's stays in the browser."
msgstr "Aplikacija, ili sajt u njenom okviru, vodi <AppProfileEntry>ličnu memoriju</AppProfileEntry> za svakog gledaoca: dokle je stiglo čitanje, šta je označeno. Ista je na svakom uređaju i čita je samo ta osoba, ne i urednici aplikacije; gostu ostaje u pregledaču."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:737
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Personal app memory"
msgstr "Lična memorija aplikacije"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1688
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Remembers for each person"
msgstr "Pamti za svakog posebno"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1316
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "The key has 1 to 64 letters, digits and the characters _ . : -."
msgstr "Ključ ima od 1 do 64 slova, cifre i znakove _ . : -."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1320
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "The value has at most 16 KB."
msgstr "Vrednost ima najviše 16 KB."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1734
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "What an app keeps for one person, nobody else reads, not even its editors."
msgstr "Ono što aplikacija čuva za jednu osobu ne čita niko drugi, ni njeni urednici."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:942
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "What one app, or a site in its frame, keeps for one profile alone, such as how far its reader got: a key and a value. Nobody else reads it, not even the app's editors, and the person sees and deletes it in the settings. An app keeps up to 100 keys per profile, each value up to 16 KB. Deleting the app, its group or the account takes them along."
msgstr "Ono što jedna aplikacija, ili sajt u njenom okviru, čuva samo za jedan profil, recimo dokle je stiglo čitanje: ključ i vrednost. Ne čita je niko drugi, ni urednici aplikacije, a osoba je vidi i briše u podešavanjima. Aplikacija čuva najviše 100 ključeva po profilu, svaku vrednost do 16 KB. Brisanje aplikacije, njene grupe ili naloga briše i njih."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:451
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "name the app gives it"
msgstr "ime koje joj aplikacija daje"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:452
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "what the app keeps"
msgstr "šta aplikacija čuva"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:450
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "whose it is"
msgstr "čija je"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1298
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Only a process drawn in Potok that starts on a signal hears the groups above and below."
msgstr "Grupe iznad i ispod čuje samo proces nacrtan u Potoku koji kreće na signal."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:402
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "hears groups above and below"
msgstr "čuje grupe iznad i ispod"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:433
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "signal from groups around"
msgstr "signal iz grupa okolo"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:921
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "A field the processes drawn in a group keep for each other: a step sets it, or adds a number to it, and every drawn process of the group reads it. It has a type, a text, a number, a yes or no, a date, a date and time, or one of its choices, and keeps a value of that type as a text. The group's editors declare it, or a drawing that sets it brings it along. A group has at most 50, each name once, and one a drawn process uses cannot be deleted. Deleting the group takes them along, and the process that wrote one last may go first."
msgstr "Polje koje procesi nacrtani u grupi čuvaju jedni za druge: korak ga postavlja ili mu dodaje broj, a čita ga svaki nacrtani proces grupe. Ima tip, tekst, broj, da ili ne, datum, datum i vreme, ili jednu od svojih stavki, i vrednost tog tipa čuva kao tekst. Zadaju ga urednici grupe, ili ga donese crtež koji ga postavlja. Grupa ima najviše 50 polja, svako ime jednom, a polje koje koristi nacrtan proces ne može da se obriše. Brisanje grupe briše i njih, a proces koji je polje poslednji upisao može da nestane pre njega."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1344
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "A text, a number, a yes or no, a date, a date and time, or a choice."
msgstr "Tekst, broj, da ili ne, datum, datum i vreme, ili izbor."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1351
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Only a choice has choices, at most 30."
msgstr "Stavke ima samo izbor, najviše 30."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:2077
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "What a process writes starts no other process: its messages and the sub-groups it makes set nothing going, so two processes never keep each other running by chance. A drawn process talks to another only by a step drawn for it. A call starts a drawn <AppProcess>process</AppProcess> that starts when another calls it, of the same group or a public one of a group above or below, and hands over what it takes; the <ValueProcess>run</ValueProcess> it starts is one level deeper, and in its own group it shares the caller's subject. A caller that waits goes on when that run ends, knowing which end it reached, or gives up at its deadline and cancels it. Cancelling a run cancels the run it waits for, and a run whose called run is cancelled stops, for an editor to take up again, which calls anew. A step can also keep a <GroupField>field of the group</GroupField>, which every drawn process of the group reads as its type; adding to one takes its lock, so two runs never lose each other's count, and a value not of its type is refused. A signal wakes the runs of the group's drawn processes that wait for it just then, at most 100, and starts the processes that start on it; nothing keeps it for a run that comes to wait later, and a wait may take only a signal sent on its own subject. A wait or a start that hears the groups above and below also takes their signals, as the entity it expects, and a run started so gets nothing of the sender's subject or people; a group beside never hears them. Runs go at most three processes deep, and a process another one of its group calls cannot be deleted."
msgstr "Ono što proces napiše ne pokreće druge procese: njegove poruke i podgrupe koje napravi ne pokreću ništa, pa dva procesa nikad ne teraju jedan drugi slučajno. Nacrtan proces razgovara sa drugim samo korakom nacrtanim za to. Poziv pokreće nacrtan <AppProcess>proces</AppProcess> koji kreće kad ga drugi pozove, iz iste grupe ili javan iz grupe iznad ili ispod, i predaje mu ono što on prima; <ValueProcess>pokretanje</ValueProcess> koje tako krene jedan je nivo dublje, a u svojoj grupi ima isti predmet kao pozivalac. Pozivalac koji čeka ide dalje kad se to pokretanje završi, znajući do kog kraja je stiglo, ili na roku odustaje i otkazuje ga. Otkazivanje pokretanja otkazuje i ono koje ono čeka, a pokretanje čiji je pozvani proces otkazan staje, dok ga urednik ne pokrene ponovo, i tada poziva iznova. Korak može i da čuva <GroupField>polje grupe</GroupField>, koje svaki nacrtani proces grupe čita kao njegov tip; dodavanje zaključava polje, pa dva pokretanja nikad ne izgube tuđe brojanje, a vrednost koja nije tipa polja se odbija. Signal budi pokretanja nacrtanih procesa grupe koja ga baš tada čekaju, najviše 100, i pokreće procese koji kreću na njega; ništa ga ne čuva za pokretanje koje kasnije stigne do čekanja, a čekanje može da primi samo signal poslat o svom predmetu. Čekanje ili pokretanje koje čuje i grupe iznad i ispod prima i njihove signale, kao entitet koji samo očekuje, a pokretanje koje tako krene ne dobija ništa od predmeta ni ljudi pošiljaoca; susedna grupa ih nikad ne čuje. Pokretanja idu najviše tri procesa duboko, a proces koji poziva drugi proces njegove grupe ne može da se obriše."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:437
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "choices of a choice"
msgstr "stavke izbora"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:436
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "type of what it holds"
msgstr "tip onoga što drži"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:2009
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "A link to a form in a <Value>value</Value> gets a card with the form's own title and subtitle, read from its settings when the value is posted. The page asks for each reader whether they may open the form: its members may, and everyone may when the form takes non-members in a public <Group>group</Group>. The others see the card a guest would get, when the group is public, and otherwise only the link. A <GroupNotice>notice</GroupNotice> reaches followers nobody asks about, so it carries only a card anyone may see."
msgstr "Link ka formi u <Value>vrednosti</Value> dobija karticu sa naslovom i podnaslovom same forme, pročitanim iz njenih podešavanja kad je vrednost poslata. Stranica za svakog čitaoca pita sme li da otvori formu: smeju njeni članovi, a svi kad forma u javnoj <Group>grupi</Group> prima i one koji nisu članovi. Ostali vide karticu koju bi dobio gost, kad je grupa javna, a inače samo link. <GroupNotice>Obaveštenje</GroupNotice> stiže pratiocima za koje niko ne pita, pa nosi samo karticu koju svako sme da vidi."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:2007
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "A link to a form shows its card to whoever may open it"
msgstr "Link ka formi pokazuje njenu karticu onima koji smeju da je otvore"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:362
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "whether the viewer sees the card of a form for its members"
msgstr "da li gledalac vidi karticu forme za njene članove"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:935
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "A template of a group's own for descriptions: the fields of a form and the HTML they go into, with tags that take them and nothing that runs. It serves its group and every group below it, and whoever may edit the group makes it there, up to 30 in a group. A description made with it keeps its HTML when the template changes, and takes the new version when it is saved again; deleting the template leaves those descriptions as they are."
msgstr "Šablon same grupe za opise: polja forme i HTML u koji ona idu, sa oznakama koje ih uzimaju i bez ičega što se izvršava. Važi u svojoj grupi i u svakoj grupi ispod nje, a pravi ga tamo ko sme da uređuje grupu, najviše 30 u jednoj grupi. Opis napravljen njime zadržava svoj HTML kad se šablon promeni, a novu verziju uzima kad se ponovo sačuva; brisanje šablona ostavlja te opise kakvi su."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:738
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Template"
msgstr "Šablon"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:460
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "name in the list of templates"
msgstr "naziv na listi šablona"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:472
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "place in the group's list"
msgstr "mesto na listi grupe"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:466
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "the HTML its fields go into"
msgstr "HTML u koji idu njegova polja"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:463
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "the fields of its form"
msgstr "polja njegove forme"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:469
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "version, which a description keeps"
msgstr "verzija, koju opis pamti"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:462
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "what it is for"
msgstr "čemu služi"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:457
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "who made it"
msgstr "ko ga je napravio"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1636
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "For a viewer who may edit its group, an app gets the <GroupTemplate>templates</GroupTemplate> of that group and of the groups above it, each with a picture of how it looks, and has Potok turn what its form holds into a description: the same HTML the group's own page writes with them. It can send pictures and videos for those descriptions too. That is how FeedCreator writes posts with an organization's own templates."
msgstr "Za onoga ko sme da uređuje njenu grupu, aplikacija dobija <GroupTemplate>šablone</GroupTemplate> te grupe i grupa iznad nje, svaki sa slikom kako izgleda, i traži od Potoka da ono što drži njena forma pretvori u opis: isti HTML koji njima piše i stranica same grupe. Može da pošalje i slike i video snimke za te opise. Tako FeedCreator piše objave šablonima same organizacije."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1634
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Writes with the group's templates"
msgstr "Piše šablonima grupe"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:455
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "its group and those below"
msgstr "njena grupa i one ispod"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:2091
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "A group's templates serve the groups below it"
msgstr "Šabloni grupe važe i za grupe ispod nje"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:2085
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "A picture a description's template takes from the device is a <Value>value</Value> in the group's chat with its <ValueAttachment>file</ValueAttachment>, so it stays among the group's files; pictures picked together for a gallery are one value with up to ten files. A video goes the same way, as it is, and plays in the description. More people see a description than a chat, so the address of the picture or video is signed and needs no login. Deleting that value also removes it from the description. A gallery says in its HTML only which pictures and in which of four looks, the one attribute of its kind the sanitizer keeps; Potok draws the look, its buttons and its counter wherever the description shows, in an app's frame too."
msgstr "Sliku koju šablon opisa uzme sa uređaja čuva <Value>vrednost</Value> u chatu grupe, sa svojim <ValueAttachment>fajlom</ValueAttachment>, pa slika ostaje među fajlovima grupe; slike koje se za galeriju izaberu zajedno su jedna vrednost sa najviše deset fajlova. Video ide istim putem, kakav jeste, i pušta se u opisu. Opis vidi više ljudi nego chat, zato je adresa slike ili videa potpisana i ne traži prijavu. Brisanje te vrednosti uklanja ih i iz opisa. Galerija u svom HTML-u kaže samo koje slike i u kom od četiri izgleda, jedinim atributom te vrste koji sanitizer pušta; izgled, dugmad i brojač crta Potok gde god se opis prikaže, i u okviru aplikacije."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:2093
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Whoever may edit a <Group>group</Group> makes its <GroupTemplate>templates</GroupTemplate>: the fields of a form and the HTML they go into, with tags that take them and nothing that runs. They serve that group and every group below it, next to Potok's own, in the description of a group and in FeedCreator, so an organization writes them once at its top. Only Potok turns them into HTML, and the sanitizer still runs over it. A description keeps the HTML and the version it was made with: a changed template reaches it only when it is saved again, and a deleted one leaves it as it is, to be edited as text."
msgstr "Ko sme da uređuje <Group>grupu</Group> pravi njene <GroupTemplate>šablone</GroupTemplate>: polja forme i HTML u koji ona idu, sa oznakama koje ih uzimaju i bez ičega što se izvršava. Važe u toj grupi i u svakoj grupi ispod nje, pored Potokovih, u opisu grupe i u FeedCreatoru, pa ih organizacija napiše jednom, na svom vrhu. Samo ih Potok pretvara u HTML, a sanitizer i dalje prolazi preko njega. Opis pamti HTML i verziju kojom je napravljen: izmenjen šablon do njega stiže tek kad se ponovo sačuva, a obrisan ga ostavlja kakav je, da se uređuje kao tekst."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1220
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "A decision gives a role, takes it, elects someone to it or ends the election of admins."
msgstr "Odluka dodeljuje ulogu, oduzima je, bira nekog za nju ili gasi izbor administratora."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1234
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "A decision that changes roles takes one answer, is put to all who may vote, is not public, and ends at a deadline, with a quorum and a majority; only an election may be won by the most votes."
msgstr "Odluka koja menja uloge prima jedan odgovor, glasaju svi koji smeju da glasaju, nije javna i završava se na roku, uz kvorum i većinu; samo izbor može da dobije onaj sa najviše glasova."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1241
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "An answer either stands for a candidate or carries a decision out."
msgstr "Odgovor je ili kandidat ili onaj koji sprovodi odluku."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1227
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Only a decision that changes roles says what came of it: done, not passed, the member left, the role is gone, the role is held through the parent, or the group would lose its last admin."
msgstr "Samo odluka koja menja uloge kaže šta je od nje bilo: sprovedena, nije prošla, član je otišao, uloge više nema, uloga je nasleđena iz nadgrupe, ili bi grupa ostala bez poslednjeg administratora."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1271
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "The root, direct conversations and threads do not elect their admins."
msgstr "Koren, direktni razgovori i niti ne biraju administratore glasanjem."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:220
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "admins come by election"
msgstr "administratori se biraju"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:602
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "candidate"
msgstr "kandidat"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:605
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "carries the decision out"
msgstr "sprovodi odluku"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:327
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "decision that gave it"
msgstr "odluka koja ju je dala"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:579
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "member it names"
msgstr "član koga imenuje"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:589
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "process run waiting for it"
msgstr "tok procesa koji je čeka"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:578
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "role it names"
msgstr "uloga koju imenuje"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:582
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "the elected one takes the others' place"
msgstr "izabrani zauzima mesto ostalih"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:584
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "what came of it"
msgstr "šta je od nje bilo"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:577
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "what the decision changes"
msgstr "šta odluka menja"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1849
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "A <Group>group</Group> that elects its admins gives and takes `admin` only by decisions of <Poll>polls</Poll>: nobody assigns it by hand, and only a decision removes an admin from the group, though an admin may leave of their own accord. An admin switches it on, and the admins it has stay for the time being, until a decision takes the role from them or an election puts its winner in their place in the same step; an election does that only when it says so, as one called from the list of members does. Only a decision switches it off, or an elected admin could stay for good. An admin inherited from the parent stays an admin. The root, direct conversations and threads do not elect their admins."
msgstr "<Group>Grupa</Group> koja bira administratore daje i oduzima `admin` samo odlukama <Poll>glasanja</Poll>: niko ga ne dodeljuje rukom, a administratora iz grupe uklanja samo odluka, mada sam može da ode. Uključuje ga administrator, a administratori koje grupa ima ostaju privremeno, dok im odluka ne oduzme ulogu ili izbor u istom koraku ne postavi izabranog na njihovo mesto; izbor to radi samo kad tako kaže, kao onaj raspisan sa spiska članova. Gasi ga samo odluka, inače bi izabrani administrator mogao da ostane zauvek. Administrator nasleđen iz nadgrupe ostaje administrator. Koren, direktni razgovori i niti ne biraju administratore."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1841
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "A <Poll>poll</Poll> may say what its decision changes: it gives a member a <GroupRole>role</GroupRole>, takes it, elects one of its candidates to it, ends the election of admins, or admits someone who asked to join. Voters read it before they vote. Such a poll is put to every member who may vote, as it says for unique and shared profiles, takes one answer, is decided by a majority with a quorum and ends at its deadline, not before; it is not opened again, and once it has a vote neither it nor its <Value>value</Value> is deleted. As it closes the decision is carried out in the same step, and the poll keeps what came of it. A <GroupMemberRole>member role</GroupMemberRole> it gave keeps the poll. A role held through the parent is not taken, and a group never loses its last admin this way either. In a group run by its founders only an admin puts such a decision to a vote; in a group that elects its admins anyone who may start a poll does. A drawn process puts one to the vote with the step that raises a poll: the decision carries the role over, as the process holds no more than `everyone`, and where the founders run the group its owner must be an admin. A request raises such a poll by the rule written down beforehand, in the name of whoever asked, and it is never deleted."
msgstr "<Poll>Glasanje</Poll> može da kaže šta njegova odluka menja: članu dodeljuje <GroupRole>ulogu</GroupRole>, oduzima je, bira jednog od kandidata za nju, gasi izbor administratora ili prima u grupu onoga ko je tražio pristup. Glasači to čitaju pre nego što glasaju. Takvo glasanje ide svim članovima koji smeju da glasaju, kako ono kaže za jedinstvene i deljene profile, prima jedan odgovor, odlučuje se većinom uz kvorum i završava se na roku, ne pre; ne otvara se ponovo, a kad ima glas, ne briše se ni ono ni njegova <Value>vrednost</Value>. Kad se zatvori, odluka se sprovodi u istom koraku, a glasanje pamti šta je od nje bilo. <GroupMemberRole>Uloga člana</GroupMemberRole> koju je dalo pamti to glasanje. Uloga nasleđena iz nadgrupe se ne oduzima, a grupa ni tako ne ostaje bez poslednjeg administratora. U grupi koju vode osnivači takvu odluku na glasanje stavlja samo administrator; u grupi koja bira administratore svako ko sme da pokrene glasanje. Nacrtan proces je stavlja na glasanje korakom koji raspisuje glasanje: ulogu prenosi odluka, jer proces nema više od `everyone`, a gde grupu vode osnivači, njegov vlasnik mora biti administrator. Zahtev raspisuje takvo glasanje po pravilu zapisanom unapred, u ime onoga ko traži, i ono se nikad ne briše."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1839
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "A decision of a poll can give and take roles"
msgstr "Odluka glasanja može da daje i oduzima uloge"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1847
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "A group may elect its admins"
msgstr "Grupa može da bira administratore"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1212
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Somebody votes: unique profiles, shared ones, or both."
msgstr "Neko glasa: jedinstveni profili, deljeni ili i jedni i drugi."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:559
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "how shared profiles vote"
msgstr "kako glasaju deljeni profili"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:611
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "one holder of a shared profile"
msgstr "glas jednog nosioca deljenog profila"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:558
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "unique profiles vote"
msgstr "glasaju li jedinstveni profili"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1264
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "A role that may go to a vote has the rules of that vote, and only then; everyone is never asked for."
msgstr "Uloga o kojoj se može glasati ima pravila tog glasanja, i samo tada; uloga „svi“ se nikad ne traži."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1257
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Admission that may go to a vote has the rules of that vote, and only then."
msgstr "Prijem o kom se može glasati ima pravila tog glasanja, i samo tada."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:216
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "how admission is decided"
msgstr "kako se odlučuje o prijemu"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:333
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "how the role is had"
msgstr "kako se dobija uloga"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:217
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "rules of a vote on admission"
msgstr "pravila glasanja o prijemu"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:334
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "rules of a vote on it"
msgstr "pravila glasanja o njoj"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1061
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "A lasting record of who admitted whom to a group and when: a member who manages requests, or a vote. It is created in the same transaction that deletes the request and creates the membership."
msgstr "Trajan zapis o tome ko je koga i kada primio u grupu: član koji upravlja zahtevima ili glasanje. Nastaje u istoj transakciji u kojoj se briše zahtev i pravi članstvo."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1068
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "A member asks for roles, saying why if it wants. It holds only the roles still waiting for whoever manages requests, one row per member and group, and goes with the membership."
msgstr "Član traži uloge i, ako hoće, kaže zašto. Drži samo uloge koje još čekaju onoga ko upravlja zahtevima, jedan red po članu i grupi, i nestaje sa članstvom."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1054
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "A profile asks to join a public group, with the roles it would like there and, if it wants, why. While a vote decides it, it names that poll. An accepted request is deleted, and an approval stays in its place."
msgstr "Profil traži pristup javnoj grupi, sa ulogama koje bi tu želeo i, ako hoće, razlogom. Dok o njemu odlučuje glasanje, pamti tu anketu. Prihvaćen zahtev se briše, a na njegovom mestu ostaje odobrenje."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1253
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "A request for roles waits for at least one role."
msgstr "Zahtev za uloge čeka bar jednu ulogu."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:756
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Decision on a request"
msgstr "Odluka o zahtevu"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:755
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Request for roles"
msgstr "Zahtev za uloge"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1245
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Someone admitted a member, or a vote did."
msgstr "Člana je primio neko ili glasanje."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1082
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "What became of admission or of one role asked for: given, refused or put to a vote, by whom (nobody when the rule put it to a vote) and why. The one who asked reads it too."
msgstr "Šta je bilo sa prijemom ili sa jednom traženom ulogom: dodeljeno, odbijeno ili stavljeno na glasanje, ko je odlučio (niko, kad je pravilo stavilo na glasanje) i zašto. Čita ga i onaj ko je tražio."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:586
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "raised by a request"
msgstr "raspisao je zahtev"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:308
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "reason given"
msgstr "navedeni razlog"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:301
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "role, none for admission"
msgstr "uloga, prazno za prijem"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:290
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "roles asked for"
msgstr "tražene uloge"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:295
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "roles still waiting"
msgstr "uloge koje još čekaju"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:307
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "vote it went to"
msgstr "glasanje na koje je otišlo"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:291
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "vote on admission"
msgstr "glasanje o prijemu"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:287
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "vote that admitted"
msgstr "glasanje koje je primilo"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:304
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "what was decided"
msgstr "šta je odlučeno"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:298
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "who asked"
msgstr "ko je tražio"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:306
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "who decided"
msgstr "ko je odlučio"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:289
#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:297
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "why they ask"
msgstr "zašto traži"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1873
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Each <GroupRole>role</GroupRole> of a statute says how it is had: nobody asks for it, whoever manages requests gives or refuses it, the same or they put it to a vote, or every request goes to a vote, whose rules the role writes down beforehand. Whoever asks reads that before sending. A member asks with a <GroupRoleRequest>request for roles</GroupRoleRequest>, which holds only what still waits; one asking to join names the roles in the <GroupJoinRequest>join request</GroupJoinRequest>, and what is left of them on admission waits as the new member's request. A role that goes to a vote raises a poll that gives it, in the name of whoever asked. Admin is given on request only by an admin, and only by a vote where the group elects its admins. Each part decided stays as a <GroupRequestDecision>decision on a request</GroupRequestDecision>, with who decided and why, and after a refusal or a vote that did not carry, the same request waits seven days."
msgstr "Svaka <GroupRole>uloga</GroupRole> statuta kaže kako se dobija: niko je ne traži, onaj ko upravlja zahtevima je dodeli ili odbije, isto to ili je stavi na glasanje, ili svaki zahtev ide na glasanje, čija pravila uloga zapisuje unapred. Ko traži, to pročita pre slanja. Član traži <GroupRoleRequest>zahtevom za uloge</GroupRoleRequest>, koji drži samo ono što još čeka; ko traži pristup, navodi uloge u <GroupJoinRequest>zahtevu za ulazak</GroupJoinRequest>, a ono što od njih ostane pri prijemu čeka kao zahtev novog člana. Uloga koja ide na glasanje raspisuje glasanje koje je dodeljuje, u ime onoga ko traži. Administratora na zahtev dodeljuje samo administrator, a u grupi koja bira administratore samo glasanje. Svaki odlučeni deo ostaje kao <GroupRequestDecision>odluka o zahtevu</GroupRequestDecision>, sa tim ko je odlučio i zašto, a posle odbijanja ili glasanja koje nije prošlo isti zahtev čeka sedam dana."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1871
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "How a role is had"
msgstr "Kako se dobija uloga"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1249
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "A change of a role names the role."
msgstr "Promena uloge navodi ulogu."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:757
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Change of access"
msgstr "Promena pristupa"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1865
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Each <GroupMemberRole>role</GroupMemberRole> given or taken, by an admin, a decision of a <Poll>poll</Poll> or an approved request, each change of a <GroupRole>role</GroupRole> of the statute or of its permissions, a <GroupManifest>manifest</GroupManifest> made or dropped, each setting of a <Group>group</Group> that lets people in, who sees an <GroupAltDescription>alternative description</GroupAltDescription>, and each member admitted, removed, blocked or gone of their own accord, with the roles they held, is written as a <GroupAccessChange>change of access</GroupAccessChange>, in the same step as the change, with who did it. What follows from these by itself, such as members coming into an inheriting sub-group, is not written, nor are invitations. Every member of the group reads the changes, and a <GroupBlock>block</GroupBlock> only those who may remove members."
msgstr "Svaka <GroupMemberRole>uloga</GroupMemberRole> data ili oduzeta, od strane administratora, odlukom <Poll>glasanja</Poll> ili po odobrenom zahtevu, svaka promena <GroupRole>uloge</GroupRole> statuta ili njenih dozvola, <GroupManifest>manifest</GroupManifest> napravljen ili napušten, svako podešavanje <Group>grupe</Group> kojim se u nju ulazi, ko vidi <GroupAltDescription>alternativni opis</GroupAltDescription>, i svaki član primljen, uklonjen, blokiran ili otišao sam, sa ulogama koje je imao, beleži se kao <GroupAccessChange>promena pristupa</GroupAccessChange>, u istom koraku kao i sama promena, sa onim ko ju je napravio. Ne beleži se ono što iz toga samo sledi, kao kad članovi ulaze u podgrupu koja ih nasleđuje, ni pozivi. Promene čita svaki član grupe, a <GroupBlock>blokadu</GroupBlock> samo oni koji smeju da uklanjaju članove."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1863
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Every change of access stays on record"
msgstr "Svaka promena pristupa ostaje zapisana"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1075
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "One change of who may do what in a group: a role given or taken, by an admin, a decision of a poll or an approved request, the statute or a setting that lets people in changed, a member admitted, removed, blocked or gone of their own accord, and who did it. It is written in the same transaction as the change. Every member reads it, blocks only those who may remove members, and deleting a profile leaves only that someone did it."
msgstr "Jedna promena toga ko šta sme u grupi: uloga data ili oduzeta, od strane administratora, odlukom glasanja ili po odobrenom zahtevu, promenjen statut ili podešavanje kojim se ulazi u grupu, član primljen, uklonjen, blokiran ili otišao sam, i ko je to uradio. Upisuje se u istoj transakciji kao i promena. Čita je svaki član, blokade samo oni koji smeju da uklanjaju članove, a kad se profil obriše, ostaje samo da je to neko uradio."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:709
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Requests, decisions and history"
msgstr "Zahtevi, odluke i istorija"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:315
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "decision that did it"
msgstr "odluka koja je to uradila"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:318
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "role it was about"
msgstr "uloga o kojoj je reč"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:317
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "what changed"
msgstr "šta se promenilo"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:321
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "what it was, in a few values"
msgstr "šta je bilo, u nekoliko vrednosti"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:309
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "who did it"
msgstr "ko je to uradio"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:312
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "whom it was done to"
msgstr "kome je to urađeno"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1855
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Every member sees who may do what"
msgstr "Svaki član vidi ko šta sme"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1857
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "The access overview of a <Group>group</Group> tells every member what each <GroupRole>role</GroupRole> of the <GroupManifest>manifest</GroupManifest> lets one do there, and why, also for roles picked together, where a denial wins over what another role allows; and what someone outside a public group, a blocked profile or a guest may. It asks the same rules the group's page does, so it cannot say anything the page does not do. It counts who holds the permissions that act on others from the <GroupMemberRole>roles</GroupMemberRole> people hold, and lists the rules of the things the member sees: <GroupAltDescription>alternative descriptions</GroupAltDescription>, <Poll>polls</Poll>, the collections of apps and the processes. Someone outside a public group sees only what they may do there and how one comes in, with no names. An admin can also open the group's page as the roles picked would see it, as a preview in which nothing changes."
msgstr "Pregled pristupa <Group>grupe</Group> kaže svakom članu šta koja <GroupRole>uloga</GroupRole> <GroupManifest>manifesta</GroupManifest> dozvoljava u grupi, i zašto, i za uloge izabrane zajedno, gde zabrana pobeđuje ono što druga uloga dozvoljava; i šta sme neko van javne grupe, blokiran profil ili gost. Pita ista pravila kao i stranica grupe, pa ne može da kaže ništa što stranica ne radi. Iz <GroupMemberRole>uloga</GroupMemberRole> koje ljudi imaju broji ko ima dozvole koje deluju na druge, i navodi pravila stvari koje član vidi: <GroupAltDescription>alternativnih opisa</GroupAltDescription>, <Poll>glasanja</Poll>, kolekcija aplikacija i procesa. Neko van javne grupe vidi samo šta on tu može i kako se postaje član, bez imena. Administrator može i da otvori stranicu grupe onako kako je izabrane uloge vide, kao pregled u kome se ništa ne menja."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:2109
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "A <GroupInvitation>group invitation</GroupInvitation> goes from profile to profile. One by email is an <GroupAccountInvitation>account invitation</GroupAccountInvitation>: it goes to whoever holds the address, and the answer to the inviter is the same whether the address has an account or not. The person picks which of their profiles accepts it, or makes a new one, and the inviter sees that profile only then; the first profile, made in the window the email's link opens, goes straight into the group of the oldest one. Either waits 30 days from when it was sent, then lapses. An invitation to a unique <Profile>profile</Profile> can also be accepted by another unique profile of the same <Account>account</Account>, or by a new one made for it, which joins in its place: the invitation then names that profile, and the inviter sees it. A <GroupJoinRequest>join request</GroupJoinRequest> goes the other way, with the roles one would like and, if one wants, why. The group's rule says who decides it: whoever manages requests, who may also put it to a vote, or always a vote. When accepted it is deleted, and an <GroupJoinRequestApproval>approved request</GroupJoinRequestApproval> stays with the name of whoever admitted the member, or the vote that did. An invitation still brings someone in at once. A member leaves of their own accord, unless they are held through the parent, which they leave instead, or are the group's last admin."
msgstr "<GroupInvitation>Pozivnica u grupu</GroupInvitation> ide od profila do profila. Poziv imejlom je <GroupAccountInvitation>pozivnica za nalog</GroupAccountInvitation>: stiže onome čija je adresa, a onaj ko poziva dobija isti odgovor, imala adresa nalog ili ne. Osoba bira koji njen profil je prihvata, ili pravi nov, i onaj ko je pozvao taj profil vidi tek tada; prvi profil, napravljen u prozoru koji otvara link iz imejla, odmah ulazi u grupu najstarije. Obe čekaju 30 dana od slanja, a onda ističu. Pozivnicu jedinstvenom <Profile>profilu</Profile> može da prihvati i drugi jedinstveni profil istog <Account>naloga</Account>, ili nov napravljen za nju, koji ulazi umesto njega: pozivnica tada nosi ime tog profila, i to vidi onaj ko je pozvao. <GroupJoinRequest>Zahtev za ulazak</GroupJoinRequest> ide u drugom smeru, sa ulogama koje bi neko želeo i, ako hoće, razlogom. Pravilo grupe kaže ko o njemu odlučuje: onaj ko upravlja zahtevima, koji ga može staviti i na glasanje, ili uvek glasanje. Kad se prihvati, briše se, a ostaje <GroupJoinRequestApproval>odobren zahtev</GroupJoinRequestApproval> sa imenom onoga ko je primio člana, ili glasanja koje ga je primilo. Pozivnica i dalje odmah uvodi u grupu. Član sam izlazi iz grupe, osim ako je nasleđen iz grupe iznad, pa izlazi iz nje, ili je poslednji administrator grupe."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1033
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "A profile invites another profile to a group. Accepting it creates the membership. An invitation to a unique profile can also be accepted by another unique profile of the same account, which it then names. One not accepted within 30 days lapses and is deleted, and the profile can be invited again."
msgstr "Profil poziva drugi profil u grupu. Prihvatanje pravi članstvo. Pozivnicu jedinstvenom profilu može da prihvati i drugi jedinstveni profil istog naloga, i ona tada nosi njegovo ime. Pozivnica koja nije prihvaćena za 30 dana ističe i briše se, a profil može ponovo da se pozove."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1793
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "A <Profile>profile</Profile> may tell its first and last name, occupation, place, phone, contact email and links, each a <ProfileField>detail</ProfileField> of its own, and its description. Each says who sees it: only the accounts that hold the profile, members of the <Group>groups</Group> it picks, anyone who is in a group with it, or anyone signed in. A group counts when both are its members, inherited too, except the root, where everyone is, direct conversations, which anyone may open, threads and an app's records. A picked group the profile leaves stops counting. A profile's card shows each viewer only what is theirs to see, and whoever the profile invites into a group, or whoever decides its request to join one, sees it as a member of that group would. Details are read on their own, never with the profile, and go with a deleted account."
msgstr "<Profile>Profil</Profile> može da kaže svoje ime i prezime, zanimanje, mesto, telefon, e-poštu za kontakt i linkove, svaki kao poseban <ProfileField>detalj</ProfileField>, i svoj opis. Za svaki stoji ko ga vidi: samo nalozi koji koriste profil, članovi <Group>grupa</Group> koje izabere, svako ko je s njim u nekoj grupi, ili svako ko je prijavljen. Grupa se računa kad su oba njeni članovi, i nasleđeno, osim korena, gde su svi, direktnih razgovora, koje svako može da otvori, niti i zapisa aplikacija. Izabrana grupa koju profil napusti prestaje da se računa. Kartica profila svakome pokazuje samo ono što je za njega, a koga profil pozove u grupu, ili ko odlučuje o njegovom zahtevu za ulazak, vidi ga kao član te grupe. Detalji se čitaju zasebno, nikad uz profil, i nestaju sa obrisanim nalogom."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:792
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "An account's face in groups: username, picture, description and details. The code does not distinguish purposes such as business, private or club. Everything that happens in a group is signed by a profile, so %{count} of the %{total} foreign keys point at this table. A profile either belongs to one account or several accounts share it. The profile of an app's process belongs to none."
msgstr "Lice naloga u grupama: korisničko ime, slika, opis i detalji. Namene kao poslovni, privatni ili klupski kod ne razlikuje. Sve što se dešava u grupi potpisuje profil, pa na ovu tabelu pokazuje %{count} od %{total} spoljnih ključeva. Profil pripada jednom nalogu ili ga deli više naloga. Profil procesa aplikacije ne pripada nijednom."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1791
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Each detail of a profile has its own audience"
msgstr "Svaki detalj profila ima svoju publiku"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1809
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Its person deletes <Account>an account</Account>, in the settings or by a link sent to its address. A <Profile>profile</Profile> only that account used stays as a deleted one, with no name, picture, description or details of theirs, and is left out wherever people are listed, mentioned or invited. Its <Value>values</Value>, <ValueAttachment>files</ValueAttachment>, <Poll>polls</Poll> and <Event>events</Event> stay in the groups, while its <GroupMembership>memberships</GroupMembership>, reactions, <GroupFollow>followings</GroupFollow>, <Tag>tags</Tag> and invitations go. A profile other accounts share stays theirs. A <Group>group</Group> where it is the only admin among people waits until someone else is made one, and one where it is alone goes with it. An account opened by an invitation nobody took up goes after 90 days."
msgstr "<Account>Nalog</Account> briše njegova osoba, u podešavanjima ili linkom poslatim na njegovu adresu. <Profile>Profil</Profile> koji je koristio samo taj nalog ostaje kao obrisan, bez imena, slike, opisa i detalja te osobe, i izostavljen je svuda gde se ljudi nabrajaju, pominju ili pozivaju. Njegove <Value>vrednosti</Value>, <ValueAttachment>fajlovi</ValueAttachment>, <Poll>glasanja</Poll> i <Event>događaji</Event> ostaju u grupama, a njegova <GroupMembership>članstva</GroupMembership>, reakcije, <GroupFollow>praćenja</GroupFollow>, <Tag>tagovi</Tag> i pozivnice nestaju. Profil koji dele i drugi nalozi ostaje njima. <Group>Grupa</Group> u kojoj je jedini administrator među ljudima čeka dok neko drugi to ne postane, a ona u kojoj je sam nestaje s njim. Nalog otvoren pozivnicom koju niko nije prihvatio nestaje posle 90 dana."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:801
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "One detail of a profile, only while it is filled: first or last name, occupation, place, phone, contact email or links. Each says who sees it: only the accounts that hold the profile, members of the groups it picks, anyone who is in a group with it, or anyone signed in."
msgstr "Jedan detalj profila, samo dok je popunjen: ime ili prezime, zanimanje, mesto, telefon, e-pošta za kontakt ili linkovi. Za svaki stoji ko ga vidi: samo nalozi koji koriste profil, članovi grupa koje izabere, svako ko je s njim u nekoj grupi, ili svako ko je prijavljen."

